---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy · Up.computer" description="How Up.computer handles information.">
  <LegalPage
    title="Privacy Policy"
    description="This policy explains what Up.computer processes when you use the app and website."
    effectiveDate="July 16, 2026"
  >
    <h2>Who operates Up.computer</h2>
    <p>
      Up.computer is operated by Kirill Gurianov. Privacy and data requests can be sent to
      <a href="mailto:support@up.computer">support@up.computer</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Local data and agent providers</h2>
    <p>
      Project files, thread history, settings, and credentials are primarily stored on your device.
      When you ask an agent to work, the content needed for that request is sent to the model or
      service provider you selected. That provider processes it under its own terms and privacy
      policy. Remote environments and websites used through Browser or Computer Use can also
      receive and observe the data you send to them.
    </p>

    <h2>Diagnostics and telemetry</h2>
    <p>
      The current public Alpha does not configure an endpoint for remote product telemetry. The app
      can create local diagnostic data, including logs and traces, to operate and troubleshoot the
      product. That data remains on your device unless you choose to share it. If remote telemetry
      is enabled in a later release, this policy will be updated before that release is published.
    </p>

    <h2>Website and third parties</h2>
    <p>
      The website and app can link to or integrate with third-party services such as GitHub, model
      providers, authentication providers, and telemetry infrastructure. Their handling of data is
      governed by their own policies. Basic server logs may include IP address, user agent, time,
      and requested path for security and reliability.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
    <p>
      Local data remains until you delete it or uninstall the relevant data directory. Service data
      is kept only as reasonably necessary for operation, security, support, and legal obligations.
      Data held by third-party providers is subject to their retention controls and policies. Send
      access, correction, or deletion requests concerning Up.computer-operated services to the
      contact above.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This policy may change as the alpha product evolves. Material updates will be published on
      this page with a new effective date.
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</Layout>
